# Personal website and Sentinel Grid frontend

Static GitHub Pages frontend for the portfolio, Sentinel MapLibre map, governance
library, synchronized monitor data, and URL Inspector client.

## Architecture

- `index.html` is the portfolio and digest homepage.
- `sentinel.html` is the operational map.
- `assets/` contains deployed CSS, JavaScript, images, fonts, and reviewed
  vendor bundles.
- `data/` contains public synchronized JSON and generated GeoJSON.
- `scripts/stage-pages.py` creates the allowlisted `_site` artifact.
- `scripts/production_gate.py` validates generated data, workflows, local links,
  artifact contents, and the 100 MiB deployment ceiling.
- `backend/url-inspector/` is the separately deployed Cloudflare Worker.

See [responsibility ownership](docs/RESPONSIBILITIES.md), [security and token
scope](docs/SECURITY.md), [performance measurements](docs/PERFORMANCE.md), and
the [operations runbook](docs/OPERATIONS.md).

## X source synchronization

Sentinel Grid owns official X API collection, retention, deduplication, and
publication. The normal monitor-state sync validates Sentinel's manifest and
publishes:

- `data/x_sources.json`
- `data/output/x_report_events.json`
- `data/output/x_report_pinpoints.geojson`

One valid report creates one GeoJSON feature and one first-class Sentinel map
event. Open map sessions check generation metadata every five minutes and
update the existing clustered source only when it changes.

## Repository secrets

`REPO_ACCESS_TOKEN` remains required only by workflows that read private source
repositories. It is not used for Sentinel or X data. Existing private
consumers may require Contents: read access to:

- `SithOperation/earthquake-volcano-discord-monitor`
- `SithOperation/EWS-discord-monitor`
- `SithOperation/ai-cyber-daily-digest`

No real value belongs in files or logs. See `docs/SECURITY.md` for rotation.

## Other synchronization workflows

`Sync Monitor States`, `Sync AI & Cyber Daily Digest`, and `Sync Early Warning
System` retain their documented schedule/manual triggers. Required private
checkouts fail visibly. `scripts/sync-monitor-data.py` validates before atomic
replacement. An invalid or malformed source never overwrites a valid website
file.

## Pages deployment and CI

`Deploy Website` runs on `main` pushes or manually. Its `validate` job runs
Python tests, frontend tests, Ruff, strict mypy, backend tests, TypeScript,
JavaScript syntax, secret scanning, browser-profile rejection, staging, link
checks, JSON/GeoJSON checks, schema/generation checks, and artifact-size checks.
The `deploy` job has `needs: validate`.

Run the local equivalents from the repository root:

```powershell
python -m pip install -r requirements-ci.txt
python -m ruff check .
python -m ruff format --check .
python -m mypy
python -m pytest
node tests/test_x_generation_refresh.js
node --test tests/test_x_report_popup.js
Push-Location backend/url-inspector
npm ci
npm test
npm run typecheck
Pop-Location
python scripts/stage-pages.py --stage _site
python scripts/production_gate.py --stage _site
```

Serve locally rather than opening HTML directly:

```powershell
python -m http.server 8000
```

## Gods Eye compatibility layer

This repository keeps Sentinel Grid as the intelligence engine and uses a compatibility adapter to normalize Sentinel data into a Gods Eye-style layer model without replacing the backend.

Key points:

- Sentinel JSON remains the canonical source for operational events.
- `assets/js/sentinel-gods-eye-adapter.js` converts raw Sentinel records into a consistent normalized shape.
- The map UI continues to use existing MapLibre rendering and public OSM tiles.
- Paid APIs are excluded. Free/public layers remain the default path.
- Optional integrations can be added later behind a graceful fallback policy.

Layer categories supported by the compatibility adapter include:

- global intelligence
- conflict
- cyber
- aircraft
- military aircraft
- maritime
- satellites
- earthquakes
- volcanoes
- weather/severe weather
- solar/space weather
- humanitarian events
- GPS interference
- internet outages

## Failure and degraded behavior

An empty X feed with `{"schema_version":"1.0","reports":[]}` is valid and
produces zero markers. Missing credentials, failed checkouts, stale/mismatched
manifests, malformed JSON, schema drift, generation mismatch, and failed output
transactions are errors. The map retains its last loaded X generation when a
browser refresh sees a cache mismatch or transient fetch failure.

Recovery and rollback procedures are in `docs/OPERATIONS.md`.

## Governance and licensing

Governance source records distinguish official sources from local companion
material. NIST SP 800-18 Rev. 2 is the current catalog record; withdrawn Rev. 1
is excluded. Missing licensed source publications remain link-only and are
listed in the governance library documentation.

Repository-authored material is all-rights-reserved; see `LICENSE.md`. Bundled
third-party components retain their own upstream licenses and notices.
